AB  - This chapter explores the integration of private blockchain technology with computational intelligence (CI) to develop advanced encryption frameworks. It introduces key terminologies and traces the evolution of blockchain, focusing on the unique security benefits of private blockchains. By incorporating CI techniques such as neural networks, fuzzy logic systems, and evolutionary algorithms, the chapter demonstrates how these methods can enhance encryption, optimize key management, and improve intrusion detection in blockchain networks. Real-world case studies from sectors like healthcare, finance, and supply chain management showcase the practical applications of these integrated technologies. The chapter also addresses challenges such as scalability, interoperability, and balancing privacy with transparency in blockchain systems. Forward looking discussions cover emerging topics like quantum-resistant encryption and the convergence of blockchain with the Internet of Things (IoT). Concluding with practical insights on deployment and future directions, this chapter serves as a comprehensive resource for professionals and newcomers, bridging theory and practice in the rapidly evolving domain of blockchain security enhanced by computational intelligence. Β© 2026 Gautam Kumar, Aditya Gupta, Gunjan and Jayeeta Chakraborty. All rights reserved.
