AB  - Quantum computing poses threats to existing cryptographic protocols like RSA and ECC. We propose QUBE-Crypto, a hybrid framework integrating Quantum Key Distribution (QKD), Post-Quantum Digital Signatures, Blockchain storage, and Pseudorandom Quantum States (PRSs). This architecture provides zero-trust authentication with provable security against classical and quantum attacks. Complexity analysis shows O(nlogn) authentication overhead with 150-260ms latency, suitable for IoT (ESP32), 5G/6G networks, and government deployments. Our system combines blockchain-secured identity registration with BB84 QKD, PRS-based challenges, and postquantum signatures (Dilithium-5, SQIsignHD), optimized for resource-constrained devices. Β© 2025 IEEE.
