AB  - The rapid development of smart cities has introduced new security challenges, necessitating advanced solutions to ensure trust, resilience, and data integrity. Blockchain technology provides a decentralized and tamper-resistant framework to enhance smart city security, enabling secure identity management, cybersecurity, critical infrastructure protection, and transparent financial transactions. This chapter explores blockchain's role in smart city security, highlighting key applications, challenges, and future research directions. While blockchain enhances security, scalability, interoperability, regulatory concerns, and high implementation costs pose significant challenges. Advancements in quantum-resistant cryptography, AI-driven security models, and decentralized governance are expected to shape the future of blockchain-enabled smart cities. By addressing these challenges, blockchain can provide a secure and transparent foundation for smart city ecosystems, ensuring long-term sustainability and efficiency. Β© 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
