AB  - Advancements in Industry 4.0 led to the tremendous expansion of the global logistics industry. Simultaneously, logistics processing is integrated by Cloud Computing, IoT (Internet of Things) devices, and Big Data Technologies. Real- time and accurate data safeguards efficient product transportation, timely delivery to customers, and effective supply chain management for the companies. The exchange of confidential customer and product data among various logistics operations stakeholders presents the risk of illegal access, which may result in fraudulent activities or the production of counterfeit goods. Hybrid cryptosystems, which include quantumresistant and classical algorithms, can be utilized to protect against both types of attacks throughout the transition phase. This chapter presents the blockchain in a post- quantum environment by adding more security layers, including multi-signature schemes with quantum-resistant hashing. This chapter proposes a hybrid technique of Blockchain and NTRUEncrypt to logistics information security. Β© 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
