AB  - The rapid growth of cloud and IoT technologies has rendered conventional encryption unsecured, particularly against novel quantum threats. To secure IoT networks with blockchain capabilities, we propose a hybrid cryptographic architecture utilizing edge computing, blockchain smart contracts, and lattice- based cryptography. Our hypothesis demonstrated that the system performed very well within controlled testing, achieving 94% storage success, 65ms latency and 99% security. In decentralized environments, the hybrid cryptographic architecture performed with minimal usage of resources while maintaining high efficiency, and ensured the secure transfer and integrity of data with scalability. In addition, it also furthers a flexible and secure foundation for future IoT applications that experience quantum threats. The next chapters in the research will investigate ways to amalgamate an even greater privacy and performance, for evolving IoT and cloud ecosystems, by looking at merging AI- infused security methods with advanced quantum cybersecurity. Β© 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
